codex
I found the concrete cause: this audit sandbox reports a namespace-local PID that has no matching `/proc/<pid>/exe`; Lean 4.22 resolves its executable through that path, so both `lean` and Lake’s install detection fail before elaboration. I’m applying a narrowly scoped audit shim that redirects only `/proc/<pid>/exe` lookups to the equivalent `/proc/self/exe`, then I’ll rerun the unchanged trusted preflight and record the shim source and hashes.
apply patch
